From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ChristopherHX <christopher.homberger@web.de>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 19:13:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] windows.ui.core.textinput: Create a CoreTextEditContext and
 let the input pane show and hide.

Xodus's patch set for GDK titles (Minecraft's among them) makes
CoreTextServicesManager::CreateEditContext return an edit context whose
methods succeed as stubs, and ICoreInputView3::TryShow/TryHide succeed.

Ported from Xodus's "add mc gdk patchset" onto WineHQ, which since took
the CoreTextServicesManager, CoreInputView stubs and the
windows.ui.text.core IDL (Alistair Leslie-Hughes): only the edit context
object and the TryShow/TryShowWithKind/TryHide successes remain. The
edit context now frees itself on its last release, is created through
core_text_edit_context_create() instead of a shared header, and
TryShow sets its result as the other two do.

Ported-from: https://github.com/xodus-gaming/wine/commit/f7331a3eaf2f0f1e7bdb94dce9379cc1a4d7bfb6
Ported: adapted
Class: feature
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-30-wine-gdk-port.md
Offered-upstream: no
